ential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+4{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =2$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5716e843d004aee90df80f9a99a117edc8c2365c713bab3e5b490fdeeedb9156"} {"question" "q-130129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "2"] ["text" "$-2$ or $2$"] ["text" "$-4$ or $2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+4{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +2)=0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-2$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5716e843d004aee90df80f9a99a117edc8c2365c713bab3e5b490fdeeedb9156"} {"question" "q-130138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{2x}+Bx{e}^{2x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-7795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{9}{4}y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-7795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{9}{4}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4}=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -\\frac{3}{2})(\\lambda -\\frac{3}{2}) & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda -\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =\\frac{3}{2}$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-7795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5716e843d004aee90df80f9a99a117edc8c2365c713bab3e5b490fdeeedb9156"} {"question" "q-7795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-7795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{-3x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+B{e}^{-x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{x/2}+Bx{e}^{x/2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-7795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-90957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+18\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+81y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-90957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+18\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+81{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+18\\lambda +81) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+18\\lambda +81=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +9)(\\lambda +9) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +9)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-9$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-9x}+Bx{e}^{-9x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-90957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5716e843d004aee90df80f9a99a117edc8c2365c713bab3e5b490fdeeedb9156"} {"question" "q-90957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-90957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-6x}+B{e}^{6x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-9x}+Bx{e}^{-9x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-9x}+B{e}^{9x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{9x}+Bx{e}^{9x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-90957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{-9x}+Bx{e}^{-9x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+9y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+9{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =3$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x}+Bx{e}^{3x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5716e843d004aee90df80f9a99a117edc8c2365c713bab3e5b490fdeeedb9156"} {"question" "q-130140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-6x}+B{e}^{6x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{3x}+Bx{e}^{3x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{6x}+Bx{e}^{6x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{3x}+Bx{e}^{3x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{9}{16}y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{3}{2}\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{9}{16}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\lambda +\\frac{9}{16}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\lambda +\\frac{9}{16}=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{4})(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{4}) & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-\\frac{3}{4}$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x/4}+Bx{e}^{-3x/4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5716e843d004aee90df80f9a99a117edc8c2365c713bab3e5b490fdeeedb9156"} {"question" "q-130143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x/2}+B{e}^{3x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x/4}+Bx{e}^{-3x/4}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x/4}+B{e}^{3x/4}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x/8}+Bx{e}^{-3x/8}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{-3x/4}+Bx{e}^{-3x/4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+4y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+4{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-2$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-2x}$ and $x{e}^{-2x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $4{e}^{-x}$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5716e843d004aee90df80f9a99a117edc8c2365c713bab3e5b490fdeeedb9156"} {"question" "q-130147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4{e}^{-2x}+x{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "4{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "6{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "x{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "{e}^{-2x}-x{e}^{-2x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-130147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{e}^{-x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-64798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the equation ${y}^{″}-14{y}^{′}+49y=0$ for $y=y(t),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-64798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}-14\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}+49{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +49) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +49 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -7)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =7$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{7t}$ and $t{e}^{7t}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $7{e}^{t}+t{e}^{7t}$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/state.json" "file_sha256" "e73e7ae59f61c6f3185b23239fe580ad4bcebe310317fb318db369ebaebca9f8"} {"question" "q-64798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063871/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5716e843d004aee90df80f9a99a117edc8c2365c713bab3e5b490fdeeedb9156"} {"question" "q-64798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/1406387